  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "VP9qWAKfMh8g14DirUuh8b7vGvw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:35.404Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Rather than instructing agents on technical routing, the agentic payment system operates on **intent principles**: agents express desired outcomes (e.g., \"Pay 50 USDC to this Solana address from my Arbitrum balance\") while professional solvers handle cross-chain routing and settlement.\n\n**Data point:** LI.FI's routing layer has handled more than **$80 billion in lifetime transfer volume across 100 million transfers**. Cross-chain settlement at scale remains one of the three open challenges, addressed by LI.FI's Solver Network and the Open Intents Framework.\n\n**Pattern:** declarative outcomes + competitive fulfillment \u2014 the same separation of *what* from *how* that makes agents composable at the tool layer, applied to money movement.\n\nSource: LI.FI, \"The Agentic Economy \u2014 A Deep Dive\" (https://li.fi/knowledge-hub/the-agentic-economy-%E2%80%94-a-deep-dive).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:35.404Z"
    }
  },
